## Hillstrom email experiment

- Source: {{ v('data.hillstrom.url') }}
- Citation: {{ v('data.hillstrom.citation') }}
- Terms: {{ v('data.hillstrom.license') }}. Kevin Hillstrom released the file in March 2008
  for the MineThatData challenge with no formal license text. It is used here for a non
  commercial portfolio with attribution, through the scikit-uplift mirror, whose MD5
  ({{ v('data.hillstrom.md5') }}) that project publishes.
- SHA-256 of the verified copy: `{{ v('data.hillstrom.sha256') }}`
- Rows: {{ v('data.hillstrom.rows') }} customers; arms of {{ v('data.hillstrom.arm.control') }} (no email),
  {{ v('data.hillstrom.arm.mens') }} (men's email) and {{ v('data.hillstrom.arm.womens') }} (women's email).
- Outcome window: two weeks. Population: recent buyers of a catalog retailer in 2008.
- Committed: `data/hillstrom/summary.json` (arm counts and outcome rates). The rows stay external.

## Online Retail II

- Source: {{ v('data.retail.url') }}
- Citation: {{ v('data.retail.citation') }}
- Terms: {{ v('data.retail.license') }}. The same source pricepoint (Day 2 of this series) priced;
  here it is the purchase history lifetime value is fit on.
- SHA-256 of the verified copy: `{{ v('data.retail.sha256') }}` (the UCI page publishes no checksum;
  a different copy fails verification on purpose so the row counts below stay tied to this file).
- Rows: {{ v('data.retail.raw_rows') }} transactions from {{ v('data.retail.first_date') }} to
  {{ v('data.retail.last_date') }}. Cleaning removed {{ v('data.retail.cancellation_rows') }} credit
  notes (invoices starting with C), {{ v('data.retail.no_customer_rows') }} rows without a customer id
  ({{ v('data.retail.no_customer_rate') }} of the non credit rows) and {{ v('data.retail.adjustment_rows') }}
  non positive adjustments, leaving {{ v('data.retail.kept_rows') }} rows,
  {{ v('data.retail.customers') }} customers and {{ v('data.retail.purchases') }} customer days.
- Windows: calibration to {{ v('data.retail.calibration_end') }}, holdout from {{ v('data.retail.holdout_start') }}.
- Committed: `data/retail/purchases.parquet` (customer id, day, revenue, lines) and `summary.json`.
  Customer ids are the dataset's own pseudonymous integers.

